guile-curl is a project that has procedures that allow Guile to do
client-side URL transfers, like requesting documents from http or ftp
servers.  It is based on the libcurl library.

If trying to build this from the repository instead of a tarball,
you'll need to run 'autoreconf -vi'.  There is a 'bootstrap' script,
but, it is just a call to 'autoreconf'.

Building from the repository requires gettext to be installed (on some
systems, the 'autopoint' package is enough).  guile-curl does not use
gettext itself.  It is needed only because Guile's own Autoconf macros
in guile.m4 (copied into m4/guile.m4) call AC_LIB_LINKFLAGS_FROM_LIBS,
which is defined in gettext's lib-link.m4.  Building from a release
tarball does not require gettext.

This is an autotools build, so usually building is a "./configure &&
make && make install" sort of thing.  It requires Guile 3.0 or 2.2 and
libcurl 7.76.0 or later.

For information on how to use it, there is a manual in the doc/
directory.

Regards,
